 "through_line": "The Udayeśvara read as historical evidence: the type and the building as it stands, with its vedī and court; the Bhūmija tower, its disputed origin, its place among Paramāra temples and between Khajuraho and the Deccan; the craft of its surfaces and the guilds behind them; the image programme set by rule and adjusted for symmetry; its damage; the texts as norms; Śaiva Siddhānta and the readings laid on the temple, ending on the temple's own inscribed words (Ch 6).",
